      "claim": "Published definitions (e.g., RFC 9110) define 'safe' as an operation that does not modify server state, and 'idempotent' as an operation where multiple identical requests have the same effect as one. An append-only log requires the write operation to be idempotent to handle at-least-once delivery, though the writer merely needs to retry, because appending modifies state (so it's not safe) but must result in exactly one append.",
